From: MinsOS <minsos@local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Backport legacy SehLights HAL code (One UI 9, y2q)

The S20+ keeps the stock SM-G986N A13 vendor light HAL. Its
ISehLights.setLightState(id, state, brightness) takes the panel level
from the int argument (x100 scale, 25500 = 1.0, HBM up to 48600) and only
falls back to ((R*77+G*150+B*29)>>8)*100 of the colour when that int is
negative (vendor.samsung.hardware.light-service 0x69fc, tbz w1,#31). The
S918B One UI 9 services always write -1 there, and above 1.0
BacklightAdapter.setBacklight hands the unpacked level over as the colour:
486 becomes 2600 and 256 becomes 0, so outdoor mode, sunlight HBM and HDR
boost drop the panel to a few nits instead of brightening it.

UN1CA's unica/patches/legacy/lights 0001 restores the A13 path but was
written for the One UI 8 smali and no longer applies (y2q build log:
"SKIP (X810 8.5): git patch did not apply cleanly"). This is the same
change re-made on the S918BXXUAZZI8 services.jar, matching what stock
A13 LightImpl.setBrightness(FI) sends:
- ISehLights$Stub$Proxy.setLightState takes the brightness int and writes
  it (same parcel as A13: id, HwLightState, int; transaction 1)
- LightImpl.setLightLocked/setLightUnchecked(color, mode, onMS, offMS,
  brightness); the (IIII) forms stay for the other callers and forward
  -1. mExtendedBrightness joins the dedupe check, as on A13
- BacklightAdapter.setBacklight always packs the colour (A13 masks with
  0xff too) and, for HwLight type 0 or 9, sends
  round(f * 255 * (USE_PERSONAL_AUTO_BRIGHTNESS_V3 ? 100 : 1));
  AUTO_BRIGHTNESS_TYPE is 4 (V3) in both the A13 and the S918B services
- PowerManagerUtil.SEC_FEATURE_USE_LIGHTS_HAL_EXTENSION is true, so
  LightsService talks to the ISehLights extension and not plain ILights
